  "text": "World War II ended in 1945, but one Japanese soldier kept fighting for another 29 years. His name was Hiro Onoda. In 1944, he was sent to a Philippine island with one order, never surrender. Then Japan lost the war. Leaflets were dropped, even messages from his family arrived, but he thought they were enemy tricks, and one by one his fellow soldiers died until he was completely alone. Then, in 1974, a young adventurer actually found him, but Onoda refused to surrender unless his commander told him to. So Japan flew his old commander to the island, and after 29 years, one order finally ended his war.",
